# 8. Objective Traceability

## Purpose

The Objective Traceability framework establishes the relationships between System Objectives and other engineering artifacts throughout the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) repository.

Its purpose is to ensure that every objective has a documented origin, defined engineering relationships, and verifiable downstream impacts.

---

## Traceability Principles

Objective traceability shall:

- Preserve engineering accountability.
- Support impact analysis.
- Enable verification and validation.
- Maintain consistency across engineering documents.
- Ensure that no objective exists without documented justification.

---

## Upward Traceability

Every System Objective shall maintain traceability to its governing sources, including:

- Project Charter.
- System Objective Specification (SOS).
- Objective Governance.

This establishes the engineering authority from which the objective is derived.

---

## Downward Traceability

Every System Objective shall maintain traceability to engineering artifacts derived from it, including:

- System Requirements.
- Engineering Architectures.
- Verification activities.
- Validation activities.

This demonstrates how objectives influence the engineering lifecycle.

---

## Horizontal Traceability

Objectives may maintain traceable relationships with:

- Related objectives.
- Supporting objectives.
- Dependent objectives.
- Cross-category objectives.

These relationships shall be explicitly documented where they contribute to engineering understanding.

---

## Traceability Rules

All traceability links shall:

- Be uniquely identifiable.
- Remain current following approved changes.
- Preserve historical records.
- Be reviewed during objective modification and retirement.

---

## Traceability Matrix

The project may maintain a traceability matrix or equivalent engineering artifact to record and manage traceability relationships across the repository.

The chosen implementation shall preserve consistency with this governance framework.

---

## Engineering Perspective

Traceability is a governance mechanism rather than an implementation activity.

Its purpose is to preserve the continuity of engineering knowledge, support informed decision-making, and maintain confidence in the integrity of the AVIA engineering repository.
